6-bit mul1 EXL3 transposed prompt kernels for shared expert 512

Adds 6-bit mul1 instantiations (`tf_exl3_prompt_gu_k12_mul1`, `tf_exl3_prompt_down_k12_mul1`
with 49,152 B dynamic SMEM) and `skip < -1` single-expert selection in `exl3_experts.cu` /
`exl3_prompt.zig`, allowing shared expert 512 to run in one 3,072-row pass right after the
512 routed 4-bit experts, reusing the same router output and rotated inputs with zero extra
scratch or split-K partials. Gated by `TF_EXL3_PROMPT_SHARED` (default 1; `0` restores
3x1024-row `grouped_body_mtl` fallback).

Verified on GB10 (Qwen3.8-Flash-Next EXL3 4.05bpw + DFlash2):
- Cold prefill 4K / 16K / 65K / 248K:
  1,933 / 1,967 / 1,937 / 1,694 -> 2,009 / 2,068 / 2,054 / 1,842 tok/s
  (248K TTFT 146.19 s -> 134.44 s, -11.75 s / +8.7%; cumulative -95.3 s vs pre-Wave-1 229.7 s)
- Exactness: 5/5 greedy, 5/5 T=0.7, and 120K needle retrieval (sha ae38468a7f52) 100% byte-identical.

